    <section class="section section--muted"><div class="shell profile-intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">In brief</p><h2>Connecting the dots is my work.</h2></div><div><p class="lede">A developer background makes it possible to speak with technical teams. Years of consulting and project management have taught me to listen to business needs, structure them and give decisions a useful frame.</p><p class="lede">Creative practice brings the same perspective: a solution should not just be produced. It needs an intention, coherence and a form people can genuinely take ownership of.</p></div><aside class="profile-intro__meta"><div><span>Location</span><strong>Nantes · France · Remote</strong></div><div><span>Languages</span><strong>French and English · C2</strong></div><div><span>Ways of working</span><strong>Consulting, design, project support, workshops</strong></div></aside></div></section>
    <section class="section"><div class="shell"><SectionHeading eyebrow="Expertise" title="Four cultures, one perspective." text="Code to understand. Consulting to decide. Creation to give form. Teaching to make work last." align="split" /><div class="service-grid service-grid--four"><article class="service-card"><span class="service-card__number">01</span><h3>Projects & consulting</h3><p>Scoping, functional analysis, estimates, planning, cross-functional coordination, reporting and client relationships.</p></article><article class="service-card"><span class="service-card__number">02</span><h3>Web & acquisition</h3><p>Fifteen years of CMS practice, especially WordPress and Gutenberg: e-commerce, HTML/CSS/JS/PHP, SEO/SEA, analytics and headless React architectures.</p></article><article class="service-card"><span class="service-card__number">03</span><h3>AI & quality</h3><p>Training, workflows and agents, data evaluation, quality control, instruction discipline and reporting.</p></article><article class="service-card"><span class="service-card__number">04</span><h3>Media creation</h3><p>Composition, audio production, editing and AI-assisted experimentation: a practice that connects intent, rhythm and finish.</p></article></div></div></section>
    <section class="section section--muted"><div class="shell"><SectionHeading eyebrow="Creative practice" title="Compose, edit, explore." text="Media creation has developed alongside digital projects. It began with conventional composition, audio and post-production tools before opening up to generative tools." align="split" /><div class="service-scope"><article><p class="eyebrow">Before generative AI</p><h3>A culture of creative tools.</h3><p>Ableton Live, Fruity Loops / FL Studio, DaVinci Resolve and the Adobe suite built a practice of composition, rhythm, editing and finish.</p></article><article><p class="eyebrow">Today</p><h3>AI as an iteration space.</h3><p>AI-assisted creation, especially music with Suno, explores directions quickly. Selection, artistic direction and coherence remain central to the work.</p></article></div><a class="text-link" href="/en/media-creation-ai/">See the media creation approach <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
